href "/event_names/58"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "4 × 400 metres Relay, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 –  7 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2106"} "Japan National Stadium, Kasumigaoka, Shinjuku, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19000475"} "71 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The United States was favored as they had the fastest set of one-lap runners, " [:em {} "Track &amp; Field News"] " noting that they had “too much firepower.” Other contenders were expected to be Jamaica and Belgium, the latter led by the Borlée brothers. As the last men’s race of the Olympics, the USA had some incentive to win as they had not won an individual running event at Tokyo, the first time that had ever happened at the Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The heats were extremely fast as all eight qualifiers bettered 3 minutes, the first time that had ever happened at a major meet. In the final " [:a {:href "/athletes/147341"} "Michael Cherry"] " led off for the USA but Botswana’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/120888"} "Isaac Makwala"] " led at the end of the first lap, recording a 43.9 leg, with Cherry and the United States second, and Trinidad &amp; Tobago’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125966"} "Deon Lendore"] " third."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147342"} "Michael Norman"] " ran the second leg for the USA, and pulled ahead on the final curve, opening up a three-metre lead on the baton pass to " [:a {:href "/athletes/147314"} "Bryce Deadmon"] ". Deadmon ran the fastest third leg, 44.01, and gave the USA a safe six-metre lead as he passed to 400 hurdler " [:a {:href "/athletes/147346"} "Rai Benjamin"] " for the anchor. Benjamin had no challenges but still ran 43.40, the fastest leg of the race, as the United States won gold in 2:55.70, the fourth fastest mark all-time."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Behind the USA the times were also fast, and a close battle brought the Netherlands home for the silver medal with a national record 2:57.18, with Botswana taking bronze, and Belgium ran a national record 2:57.88 to finish fourth. Botswana had run 2:57.27, both a national and African record."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:57.77 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2:55.70 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/147341"} "Michael Cherry"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147342"} "Michael Norman"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147314"} "Bryce Deadmon"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147346"} "Rai Benjamin"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147354"} "Trevor Stewart"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147347"} "Randolph Ross"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/147355"} "Vernon Norwood"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Netherlands"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "2:59.06 (5 h1)"] [:td {} "2:57.18 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/125054"} "Liemarvin Bonevacia"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/145549"} "Terrence Agard"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/145550"} "Tony van Diepen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/145546"} "Ramsey Angela"] " 